            <div xml:id="d729">

                <pb facs="0696" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg606"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/894</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Moscow</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-01-08T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 8,
                                1918, 7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your 139, December 28 [29], 1 p.m. Only instructions for you at present other
                    than those already sent December [January] 5 as to leaving Moscow are to keep
                    Department fully advised.</p>
                <p>Appreciate value of Poole’s report and
                    your comment. Send Jenkins’s report
                    soonest possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
